WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:11.500
[Music]

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.000
[Suspenseful Music] [Little boy playing with baseball bat.]

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.000
[Tires screech, woman steps out of car gasping.]

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:32.480
[Music]

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:41.000
[Woman walks with child into the store, chatting]

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:49.040
[Shopkeeper chuckles.]

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:52.140
[Sam:] Oh, you women. That wasn't even a near- miss.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.900
[Linda Thorpe:] I sound like a bozo. I think I better sit down.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:57.100
[Sam:] All right. Hiya, Johnny.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:02.100
Well, come sit down then, Linda. There you are.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.160
You know, kids do kind of scare you at that.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:10.040
[Linda Thorpe:] Who is he?

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:14.320
[Sam:] Miss Thorpe, I would like to have you know Master Johnny Walsh.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:19.780
Son, I'd like to present Miss Linda Thorpe, our public health nurse.

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:21.760
[Linda Thorpe:] Well, how do you do, Johnny.

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:23.880
I'm very happy to know you.

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:26.340
[Johnny Walsh:] Pleased to meet you, ma'am.

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.760
[Linda Thorpe:] You're new around here, aren't you?

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.980
[Sam:] Yeah. They moved into the county about, oh, about a week ago.

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:34.660
His folks took over the big old Staley place.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:38.480
Well, they've got a big family, haven't you, Johnny?

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:40.940
[Johnny Walsh:] Got a sister two years older than me.

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:42.260
[Linda Thorpe:] You have?

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:46.920
[Sam:] Yup. You've got two sisters, and they're expecting a new baby for Christmas.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:48.220
[Linda Thorpe:] Oh, how nice.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:52.860
You know, I'd like to meet your mother and your father and your sisters, too.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:54.780
[Johnny Walsh:] But they're just girls.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:57.660
[Linda Thorpe:] They're just girls? Ha ha ha.

00:01:58.520 --> 00:01:59.460
A new baby by Christmas.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:00.900
Well, you don't have long to wait, do you?

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.740
[Sam:] Not nearly as long as your folks have been waiting for you

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.900
to bring the groceries home for supper.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.820
[Laughter]

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.120
All right, Johnny. Here you are.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:13.920
[Linda Thorpe:] Oh. Maybe I better help you with this. You going my way, Johnny?

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:15.800
Well, I'll take you in my car, then.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:18.900
[Sam:] It might be a good idea to get your car off the road, too, Linda.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.600
[Linda Thorpe:] Yeah, it sure is. Can you get down? Okay.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:23.900
Well, I'll see you, Sam.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.400
[Sam:] All right, bye bye Linda.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:26.900
[Sam:] Bye bye, Johnny.
[Johnny Walsh:] Bye.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.060
[Music]

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:33.500
[Narrator:] It was as simple as that.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:39.200
A little boy playing by the road, and a public health nurse making her daily rounds.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:43.400
But that is how the local health department first met the Walsh family.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:47.920
They'd just moved in and were still working hard to get their home in order.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.900
They weren't quite ready to welcome visitors.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:03:04.660
[Music]

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:08.800
Ms. Linda Thorpe was a qualified public health nurse, and an important part of her job

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:15.500
was to know how to make an unexpected call like this seem as natural as possible.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:23.280
Yes, it always takes a few minutes to get over that first awkward feeling,

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:26.800
that feeling of being ill at ease and self-conscious.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:31.900
Linda also knew that smiling children could open doors of friendship to their parents.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.600
And when an eager invitation to see the new kittens was offered,

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:41.500
Linda felt sure that these people would soon be her friends.

00:03:41.880 --> 00:04:10.000
[Music]

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:14.740
Although hardly a word had been spoken, Linda knew that she had once again

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.980
made friends of strangers.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:21.440
Now she could explain the work she was doing and why the local health department

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:26.000
maintains a nursing service, to help us all keep well.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:32.000
As part of her work, Linda asked about the baby that was expected in December.

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:34.820
Mary Walsh hadn't been to see a doctor yet.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:39.800
They'd been so busy fixing up the house, and she felt it could wait.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.140
Besides, she hadn't had any trouble with the other children.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:48.340
But Linda explained that where there are other children in the family,

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:51.460
you can never afford to put off seeing a doctor.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:56.840
[Music]

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:02.300
Mary was easily persuaded to visit the doctor sooner than she had planned.

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:09.700
A few days later, she went to a local doctor for a complete physical examination.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:14.400
She also had a chest x-ray, something which should be part of the routine examination

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.960
of every expectant mother.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:24.600
In most patients, nothing unusual is found, but in Mary's case, the doctor discovered a small shadow

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:25.940
on one of her lungs.

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:33.880
It might mean very little, but often, it's the only means of discovering early tuberculosis,

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:39.040
because early TB has no obvious symptoms.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:41.600
It is often unsuspected.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:50.820
Mary was called back for further tests, for no diagnosis is complete

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:54.120
until specific laboratory tests are made.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:06:00.700
Every technique of modern medicine is put to work until the diagnosis is confirmed or denied.

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:07.580
Mary Walsh didn't even feel sick, yet she had tuberculosis.

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:12.920
Now she became a responsibility of the community, and the community went to work

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:14.580
to help her get well.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:18.660
[Music]

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:22.320
[Jim Walsh:] Mary and I've done nothing but talk about this since we first read these.

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:25.740
[Linda Thorpe:] Now you know why it's best for you to go to the hospital.

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:29.020
[Mary Walsh:] You know, we can't afford a big hospital bill.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.800
[Linda Thorpe:] It won't cost what you think.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:36.220
[Jim Walsh:] I know you mean well, but we can't accept charity.

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:37.980
[Linda Thorpe:] No one's offering you charity.

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:43.720
Like the schools, your tuberculosis hospital is part of the local government that you help support.

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:46.820
Its job is to keep the community healthy.

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:51.840
Why, by helping you, the community is also protecting itself.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:55.400
[Mary Walsh:] But we don't even have enough to pay someone to come look after the children

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:56.760
if I'm not here.

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:58.620
We have no close relations near here.

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:04.500
Jim is a good man, but he can't do everything by himself.

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:10.000
[Linda Thorpe:] Miss Swain of our welfare department is good at that sort of thing.

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:12.400
She'll help you find a way.

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:15.800
[Mary Walsh:] You make it all sound so simple.

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:18.980
But what about the new baby?

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:23.100
[Linda Thorpe:] Your baby won't catch tuberculosis from you if you do what the doctor tells you.

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:25.800
But no case of TB is simple.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:29.500
You're more fortunate than some because your case was caught early.

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:32.900
[Jim Walsh:] Just how long do you think it'll take in my wife's case?

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:37.400
[Linda Thorpe:] No one can say for sure, but Mrs. Walsh should stay in the hospital

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:39.600
at least until after the baby is born.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:42.900
[Mary Walsh:] But that won't be for months. I won't do it.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:49.500
[Linda Thorpe:] I know this is a shock, but when you think of the children as well as yourself,

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:52.220
I know you'll want to do the sensible thing.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:56.880
[Jim Walsh:] We both want to do what's right.

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:01.800
[Linda Thorpe:] Well, hello Jane and Nancy, too.

00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:02.800
Been playing hard?

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:03.440
[Jane:] Yes.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:07.200
[Linda Thorpe:] Oh, and there's my pal. How are you, Johnny. Haven't seen you for a long time.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:13.540
[Music]

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:16.940
[Mary Walsh:] Yes. And I must protect the children.

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:19.900
[Linda Thorpe:] Exactly, and the new baby most of all.

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:25.800
You need rest and care now, good food, a place where there are doctors and nurses,

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:27.100
the right medicine.

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:30.900
You can only get that kind of care in a hospital.

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:38.980
[Narrator:] Leaving her family for the first time in her life was made easier for Mary Walsh

00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:40.200
by many helping hands.

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:46.100
Arrangements had been made for Mrs. Spencer to come and stay at home with the children

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:50.080
and take good care of them while their mother was to be away.

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:54.660
[Music]

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:59.200
Miss Swain of the welfare department had made all the plans and preparations to keep the family

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:01.120
as happy as possible.

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:09.600
Mary didn't know just where or how she had gotten tuberculosis, but she knew she had to go away.

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:14.100
To protect her children, she had to leave them for a while until she was cured.

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:21.680
And as she looked at them, she wanted to do everything she could to speed her own recovery

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:26.100
and return to her family well and happy.

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:34.700
[Music]

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:40.300
The tuberculosis hospital wasn't far from home, and here Mary could have complete rest in bed.

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:44.300
More than that, there was a skilled staff who took a personal interest in her.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:49.100
She knew that she had the best medical attention in the world, and she didn't have to

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:50.900
worry about her family,

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:53.700
so she could keep her mind at rest.

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:57.200
This is so important in curing tuberculosis.

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:06.140
[Music]

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:11.020
Linda made arrangements for the health department to examine the rest of the family

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:14.680
right away to make sure that no one else was sick.

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:17.000
This was one of the many public health services in the community

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:21.700
which the local Tuberculosis Association had worked hard to establish.

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:30.040
[Music]

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:31.980
The children are treated with special care,

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:36.000
for more than medical skill is required to make it all seem to them

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:38.500
like a natural part of a big adventure.

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:50.400
[Music]

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:53.880
Jim Walsh was also examined with the latest x-ray equipment obtained with help

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:56.900
from the local Tuberculosis Association.

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:02.940
When the test showed that none of the others had active TB, the family began to readjust itself,

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:07.880
with the help of Miss Swain of the welfare department, who offered friendly suggestions

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:11.040
on how to manage the house while mother was away.

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:16.300
[Music]

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:20.300
The weeks passed. Mary was busy and content.

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:25.900
She knew that her family was well-taken care of, especially the children.

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:29.200
Nellie Spencer, was wonderful with the youngsters.

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:34.800
[Music]

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:39.300
And such peace of mind helped to speed the progress of her recovery.

00:11:41.020 --> 00:11:45.400
It was comforting to know the farm was doing nicely, that things were good at home.

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:52.840
As Mary grew stronger and healthier, she began to sit up and prepare for the day

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:54.900
when the baby was due.

00:11:56.980 --> 00:12:00.200
Jim Walsh, too, was counting the weeks and then the days.

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:39.000
[Music]

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:42.200
Congratulations. It's a boy.

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:43.900
Mother doing fine.

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:52.800
It was a healthy baby boy, and he was at home now with the rest of the children, growing fast, too.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:55.800
Mary knew she was getting better.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:58.600
She'd soon be allowed on her feet,

00:12:58.820 --> 00:13:01.700
and then she'd be able to walk around.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:04.600
That was almost like being home.

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:08.860
Already they were making plans for her return.

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:13.980
Mrs. Benson, the home demonstration agent, came in to show Jim how to make it simple and easy

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:17.100
for Mary to do the housework when she came back.

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:20.360
She should not be allowed to overwork.

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:24.780
It was important to keep her from reaching, bending, or stretching too much.

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:29.020
[Music]

00:13:29.020 --> 00:13:33.960
Yes, everything was being done so that Mary's work would be easier.

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:36.300
Everyone was learning to do his share.

00:13:38.820 --> 00:13:42.900
They're all getting ready to do their own special jobs.

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:49.600
[Music]

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:55.700
On his regular visits, Jim saw Mary's steady progress, and told her how the baby was growing.

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:01.500
This was no ordinary farewell.

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:03.480
Mary was on her feet again.

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:08.400
The day wasn't far off now when they would all be walking together.

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:15.280
Then one day Linda Thorpe was able to tell Nellie the good news.

00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:18.300
Very soon now, Mary would be coming home.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:23.900
The final touches for the homecoming were made.

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:28.700
[Music]

00:14:28.980 --> 00:14:31.600
Mother, was home again.

00:14:31.820 --> 00:14:52.800
[Music]

00:14:52.940 --> 00:14:56.380
And now the public health nurse moves on.

00:14:57.020 --> 00:15:00.640
To help the many others who need her care and attention.

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:06.400
She is a symbol of the community's continuing effort to keep its people well.

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:10.080
But she knows that these are more than just her neighbors.

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:18.200
These are her friends. This is her community, and these are her people.

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:30.220
[Music]

